ection against shortages roughly equals the extra storage cost for item 0. For item 1, storage costs more than the protection is worth, at roughly −50.\n- **Candidate 0** has a moderate starting buffer (+15 / +12) and a mild cut at the end. It sits between the two and comes out slightly ahead of candidate 3.\n\n**The rest are clearly worse**\n- **Candidate 7** (about 1.1 × forecast) buys about 38 extra units of item 0 and 55 of item 1. Many of them sit in storage or are left over at the end. Overall it is roughly 200 below candidate 0.\n- **Candidate 6** (about 1.2 × forecast) builds up much more surplus. Purchases, storage and leftovers cost a lot.\n- **Candidate 1** (about 0.95 × forecast) orders less than demand, so it loses many sales at 27 / 18 each.\n- **Candidates 2 and 4** order every two days, which saves about 350 in daily order fees. But each delivery covers two days, so the second day's stock sits overnight: about 650 in extra storage. Candidate 4 also orders less than demand overall. Candidate 2 has the same surplus as candidate 7.\n\n**Under random demand:** candidate 0's buffer protects it from the start. Its total purchases are close to mean demand, so it neither runs short for long nor piles up leftovers."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 352, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 352}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T06:59:42.686Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBABCFdBoCBVXdybwsdu"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content